        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "ci(qa): reuse Matrix live workflow for releases",
        "body": "Stack 3 of 4. Depends on #103589.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nRelease checks duplicate the Matrix live-lane setup instead of calling the\nmaintained QA Lab live-transport workflow, while manual full Matrix proof and\nrelease proof can drift in trust validation, retry, artifact, and status\nsemantics.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMake `QA-Lab - All Lanes` reusable with exact-ref validation and explicit lane\ninputs, then route the release Matrix profile through that workflow and consume\nits status output. Manual `matrix_profile=all` continues to fan out the five\nbounded profiles so the 92-scenario proof stays within per-job timeouts.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRelease maintainers get one Matrix live-lane implementation for focused release\nproof, with deterministic mock-provider inputs and explicit status propagation.\nManual full Matrix validation keeps its parallel transport, media, and E2EE\ncoverage.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm test test/scripts/package-acceptance-workflow.test.ts`: 45/45 tests\n  passed on Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kx5mgn8jwgz9a3skm5e2g4gn`.\n- `node scripts/check-workflows.mjs`: pinned actionlint fallback, zizmor, and\n  workflow interpolation guards passed on the same Testbox.\n- Autoreview caught the initial loss of manual `all` fanout; the fanout was\n  restored with direct contract coverage, and the fresh rerun completed clean\n  with no accepted/actionable findings.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n",
